# Jasmine Sambac project — live inventory parse

> Mixing-order clarification, 2026-09-08: the category groups in this initial parse are inventory text sections, not the user's 17 physical baskets. The current [V2 basket card](../../formulas/Jasmine_Sambac_Clair_30mL_V2_Baskets_1-17.md) follows the saved Basket 1–17 convention, including Benzyl Benzoate and Hexyl Salicylate in Basket 1. Do not use this historical category grouping as the pouring order.

> Latest correction, 2026-09-08: **Romandolide is now DEPLETED**, confirmed by the user. Live counts are 240 raw rows, five depleted, 235 not marked depleted. The original four-depleted snapshot below is retained as history, not current dosing authority. The formula has a stock-corrected V2 successor.

> Post-parse correction, 2026-09-08: the user confirmed the Sambac absolute stock is **10% w/w in DPG**. PerfumersWorld identifies **Jasmine Sambac Blossoms, 6JN07707, as a liquid proprietary jasmine base**, not dried flowers. The dried-flower interpretation below was inherited from an incorrect inventory comment and is superseded. The source hash and full row list in this report describe the initial snapshot, before these two inventory corrections. See [stock clarifications](Jasmine_Sambac_Stock_Clarifications_2026-09-08.md). The companion JSON preserves the original parse for provenance, not current dosing authority.

Date: 2026-09-08. Scope: parse and reconcile the current worktree inventory before selecting or dosing the 30 mL perfume.

## Source and authority

- Source: `C:\Users\ASUS\.codex\worktrees\52e4\perfume-chem\inventory.txt`
- SHA-256: `DF5421C5B013330375A1856CCCD6AFCEB2382A1519135BC0C63579CB6441AA0B`
